  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieves 0.4348 acc, only marginally above RNA-only scgpt (config_031, 0.4106), while image-only is weak (0.2266). This small multimodal gain (~0.024) raises the question of whether the concat fusion is suboptimal and suppressing the image contribution. Question tested: config_032 is identical to config_001 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, isolating the effect of the fusion mechanism on how well the (weaker) image branch contributes. Why best next step: It is the cleanest single-variable comparison available, directly addressing whether the modest multimodal advantage can be amplified by a learned weighting scheme. If weighted fusion meaningfully improves accuracy, it justifies further investment in fusion/aggregation design; if not, it indicates the image modality's contribution is inherently limited and effort should shift to RNA encoder choice or image encoder selection. This is more informative than jumping to multiprofile or changing the RNA encoder, which would conflate multiple variables."
}

